# Frontend (React + Tailwind)

## Theme & brand (configurable)
- Colors come from the root `.env` (`VITE_THEME_BG`, `VITE_THEME_SURFACE`, `VITE_THEME_TEXT`, `VITE_THEME_ACCENT`) and are exposed as CSS variables + Tailwind tokens. Default dark theme: bg `#000000`, text `#ffffff`, accent `#8EFF19`.
- Never hardcode brand strings. Read brand name/motto from `src/config/brand.js` (backed by `VITE_BRAND_NAME`, `VITE_BRAND_MOTTO`).
- Logo is a single configurable PNG at `src/assets/logo.png`, referenced via `src/config/brand.js`. Swapping the file changes the logo everywhere.

## Structure & reuse
- Modular: shared UI in `src/components/`, pages in `src/pages/`, layouts in `src/components/layout/`.
- Reuse the Reback template's look (adapted to CTRL dark theme) — re-implement pages like `SignIn2` in React, don't copy Blazor files.
- Auth token stored client-side and attached as `Authorization: Bearer` on every API call via `src/lib/api.js`.

## i18n & RTL
- **Translations live ONLY in the database** (`translations` table, namespace `ui`), served by `GET /i18n/{locale}` and loaded at boot via `loadDbTranslations()` in `src/i18n/index.js`. There are **NO `en.json` / `ar.json` files** — never (re)create them or import bundled locale JSON.
- To add/change a UI string: insert/update the row in the DB. For fresh installs, also add it to the `translations` seed in `database/db.sql` (the DB is the source of truth). All keys still go through `t()` with dotted keys (e.g. `categories.errors.nameEnTaken`).
- Backend validation errors should return the i18n **key** as the `detail`; the frontend translates it with `t(detail, { defaultValue: detail })`.
- When language is Arabic, set `dir="rtl"` on `<html>` and ensure components mirror correctly (use logical spacing utilities / `rtl:` variants). Adding a new language = add an entry to `LANGUAGES` and seed its rows in the DB.

## Data ordering
- List/retrieval endpoints return records in **ascending alphabetical (A–Z) order by name** by default (e.g. categories by `name_en`, suppliers by `name`), unless the feature exposes an explicit sort control (e.g. the products list) or a deliberate admin-defined `sort_order` (e.g. attributes).

## UX
- Show the `Preloader` on initial load / route auth checks.
- Protect routes: unauthenticated users are redirected to `/login`; authenticated land on `/dashboard`.
